  "id": "coldshoulder",
  "neon": "#8fe3ff",
  "note": "COLD SHOULDER — the ice house on Meltwater Row.\n\nThe tile's prose: no shopfront and no window at street level, just a door reveal deep enough to\nstand in out of the rain (brick, then cork, then boards, three feet of wall), COLD SHOULDER cut into\nthe lintel and painted white every spring, and the gable end running out over the Basin on piles,\nwith a gantry bolted through it that drips all year.\n\nSo the street face is a tall blind brick wall with brick piers and three insulation bands showing\nas string courses, and one door set in a deep projecting surround with the name cut into its\nlintel. The back carries the gantry: a beam out over the water on the gable end, with the drip\nrunning down the wall under it. One cold lamp over the door is the only light.",
  "pal": "ty_oc_brick",
